2. Wired into v2.5.38. The ergosphere and virtues sit on the existing intent forces, so the velocity damp stays frame-rate independent and the matrices are untouched.

What changed:

Spawn — each pedestrian gets gi (0.8), yu (random courage), and laneX.
Ergosphere — radius grows with speed and heat. Ahead and inside it: low yu panics to the outer lane, high yu pins to laneX, everyone else gets a clamped lateral push. Sea and visit goals are left alone.
Jin — if a family member shifts lane, siblings follow, rate-limited to once per 0.45 s so it doesn't cascade.
Gi — scales the existing lane spring. No raw dt lerp, so no snap.
QNH — higher heat raises the chance of random lane changes, capped at 0.7.

Open the file on your phone and run. Low-courage people should peel off early, high-courage ones should hold their line.

